From 948deba873343e77956866057a1a524a227ed7eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Theorem Labs
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:45:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [asan] intercept pthread_tryjoin_np and pthread_timedjoin_np
 on musl
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

🤖: ASan intercepts pthread_tryjoin_np and pthread_timedjoin_np only on
glibc.  asan_interceptors.h:105-110 sets ASAN_INTERCEPT_TRYJOIN and
ASAN_INTERCEPT_TIMEDJOIN to 1 only when SANITIZER_GLIBC and
ASAN_INTERCEPT_PTHREAD_CREATE are both true.  musl defines both functions
with weak_alias (src/thread/pthread_join.c:38-39), and include/pthread.h
declares them with glibc's arguments (lines 227-228).  So a static musl
program's calls of these two functions go straight to libc.

ASan uses these interceptors to find a second join of a thread.  ASan
keeps a record of each joinable thread in ThreadArgRetval
(sanitizer_thread_arg_retval.cpp).  The interceptors of
pthread_join, pthread_tryjoin_np and pthread_timedjoin_np call
asanThreadArgRetval().Join() (asan_interceptors.cpp:290-333).  When the
join succeeds, Join() calls AfterJoin(), which removes the record.  On a
later join of the same thread, ThreadArgRetval::BeforeJoin finds no
record.  It then reports "Joining already joined thread, aborting." and
stops the program.  It does this when detect_invalid_join is set, and
that flag is on by default (sanitizer_flags.inc:283).

Without this patch, a successful pthread_tryjoin_np or
pthread_timedjoin_np on musl does not call Join().  ASan keeps the
thread's record, so it does not report a second join of that thread.
The second join is undefined behaviour.

Check musl as well: the condition becomes
(SANITIZER_GLIBC || SANITIZER_MUSL) && ASAN_INTERCEPT_PTHREAD_CREATE.
Then ASan reports a second join after a successful pthread_tryjoin_np or
pthread_timedjoin_np on musl, as it does on glibc.

The second half of the change is in sanitizer_platform_interceptors.h.
SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_TRYJOIN and SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_TIMEDJOIN (lines
406-407) become (SI_GLIBC || SANITIZER_MUSL).  These two gates hold the
same two interceptors of standalone LSan (lsan_interceptors.cpp:497-525),
which call the same Join().  HWASan sets both gates to 0 itself
(hwasan_platform_interceptors.h:518-522).  No other runtime reads them.

On 32-bit Arm, musl's include/pthread.h:237 sends calls of
pthread_timedjoin_np to __pthread_timedjoin_np_time64.
asan_interceptors.cpp includes sanitizer_common_interceptors.inc at line
204, before its own interceptor at line 325.  So the renames at the top
of that .inc (lines 164-232) apply to it too, and on armv7 ASan attaches
the interceptor as __pthread_timedjoin_np_time64.  lsan_interceptors.cpp
does not include the .inc, so standalone LSan keeps the plain name.
pthread_tryjoin_np takes no time argument and keeps its name on every
target.

Like patch 0030, this patch changes libclang_rt.asan.a.  A toolchain that
has it is a new toolchain version.

Line numbers in this message are those of llvmorg-20.1.8 and of musl
f21a9653.
---
 compiler-rt/lib/asan/asan_interceptors.h                     | 2 +-
 .../lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_platform_interceptors.h   | 5 +++--
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/compiler-rt/lib/asan/asan_interceptors.h b/compiler-rt/lib/asan/asan_interceptors.h
index 3e2386eaf..98aa55d39 100644
--- a/compiler-rt/lib/asan/asan_interceptors.h
+++ b/compiler-rt/lib/asan/asan_interceptors.h
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ void InitializePlatformInterceptors();
 # define ASAN_INTERCEPT___STRDUP 0
 #endif
 
-#if SANITIZER_GLIBC && ASAN_INTERCEPT_PTHREAD_CREATE
+#if (SANITIZER_GLIBC || SANITIZER_MUSL) && ASAN_INTERCEPT_PTHREAD_CREATE
 # define ASAN_INTERCEPT_TIMEDJOIN 1
 # define ASAN_INTERCEPT_TRYJOIN 1
 #else
diff --git a/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_platform_interceptors.h b/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_platform_interceptors.h
index 11914c9c0..213f6ea8e 100644
--- a/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_platform_interceptors.h
+++ b/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_platform_interceptors.h
@@ -408,8 +408,9 @@ SANITIZER_WEAK_IMPORT void *aligned_alloc(__sanitizer::usize __alignment,
   (SI_LINUX_NOT_ANDROID || SI_SOLARIS)
 #define SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_PTHREAD_BARRIERATTR_GETPSHARED \
   (SI_LINUX_NOT_ANDROID && !SI_NETBSD)
-#define SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_TRYJOIN SI_GLIBC
-#define SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_TIMEDJOIN SI_GLIBC
+// musl has pthread_tryjoin_np and pthread_timedjoin_np too.
+#define SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_TRYJOIN (SI_GLIBC || SANITIZER_MUSL)
+#define SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_TIMEDJOIN (SI_GLIBC || SANITIZER_MUSL)
 #define SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_THR_EXIT SI_FREEBSD
 #define SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_TMPNAM SI_POSIX
 #define SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_TMPNAM_R (SI_GLIBC || SI_SOLARIS)
